FormalShell for Debian and Ubuntu
=================================

The user units are installed but not enabled, since they would start the
shell in any graphical session. Enable them for your user:

    systemctl --user enable formalshell.service formalshell-watchdog.timer

Hyprland's binds and layer rules for the shell ship as a Lua file. Load it
from ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua:

    dofile("/usr/share/formalshell/examples/hyprland/formalshell.lua")

formalshell-power-poll.service, which feeds USB-C and CPU draw to the power
panel, is enabled on install.

